// @emit-error an i32-keyed Map/Set is supported as a binding / parameter / return / `| null` / an ARRAY ELEMENT at any depth / a closure result / a MAP VALUE / a struct or variant FIELD — not inside
// CAPABILITY: the map as a UNION MEMBER — the one position left, and now the one the
// message names as such.

// A union spelling reaches `i32MapSpellingLowerable` as ONE `TypeRef`, and its arm accepts a
// member that is a struct ARM carrying the map in a FIELD (`{f: {[i32]: V}} | i32`, which
// `i32-keyed-variant-field.vl` runs) because the field ROW carries the key. A member that IS
// the map does not: it lowers into the shared BOX (`{tag, value}` with an `anyref` payload),
// and nothing there records which of the two map structs the payload holds.

// THAT ARGUMENT IS NOW MEASURED, NOT REASONED. Opening this arm along with the other three
// container positions made THIS program `vl check` rc 0 and then invalid wasm —
// `type mismatch: expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)` — so the `is`-narrowed read
// really does cast to whichever struct the member name scan claimed. The arm was re-closed and
// the question filed: `open-rulings.md` §B6a-map-in-union-box, options and a recommendation.

// The one-line difference from the accepted form is the absence of a field name:
//   `{f: {[i32]: i32}} | i32`   accepted — the map is a FIELD of an arm
//   `{[i32]: i32} | i32`        this file — the map IS the arm
const m: {[i32]: i32} = Map()
m[1] = 7
const u: {[i32]: i32} | i32 = m
if u is {[i32]: i32} { print(u.length) } else { print(-1) }
